{"meta":{"format_version":"5.0","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"wall_stone_broken","model_identifier":"wall_stone_broken","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","multi_file_ruleset":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# wall_stone_broken\n\nDamaged state below 40 % HP of `wall_stone` (Patch 5): the stone piece snapped in half, with splinters (or broken stone) at the break and the upper half (group `hanging_half`) still attached by a thread, hanging down to rest on the ground in front (-Z). Purely visual: the hanging half does not block movement and the wall works the same. The game swaps it in below 40 % HP and back to `wall_stone_cracked` when repaired above 40 %.\n\nStone wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Stone: grey blocks, 3.6 m (128 u), one merlon, a walkway on top.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -12..15, y 0..69, z -62..10 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material (repainted in Patch 5 for colour contrast).\n- Cubes: 21, all in `finished`; the construction and ruined state sets and the damaged/abandoned texture variants were removed in Patch 5 (the game draws none of them for buildings).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 128 x 16 centred at x 0, z 0\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 119, 2)"},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":256},"elements":[{"name":"stone_wall_merlon#aba79d","box_uv":false,"render_order":"default","locked":false,"export":true,"scope":0,"allow_mirror_modeling":true,"from":[-4,118,-8],"to":[4,128,-4],"autouv":0,"color":0,"origin":[0,0,0],"faces":{"north":{"uv":[132,124,140,134],"texture":0},"east":{"uv":[148,124,152,134],"texture":0},"so